			<div class="content" id="post-content-3301134">
									

<p>Working on a fix for you, almost got it&#8230;</p>
<p>&#8230;okay, in the hidden stuff part, right below</p>
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>&lt;canvas style=&quot;position:absolute;width:800px;height:400px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;</code>
</pre></div>
<p>change those lines to</p>
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>&lt;input id=&quot;password&quot; input=&quot;&quot; style=&quot;position:absolute;width:200;height:100;top:300px;left:410px;background:transparent;color:#7CFC00;border: solid 1px; border-color:#7CFC00&quot; type=&quot;text&quot;&gt;
&lt;input value=&quot;&quot; name=&quot;submit&quot; style=&quot;position:absolute;top:300px;left:560px;background:transparent;border:none;&quot; type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;</code>
</pre></div>
<p>You can change &quot;border:none;&quot; or the background color on the second one if you don't want the submit button to be invisible.</p>
<p>Explanation: At least for me the problem was that the password thingy was trying to appear in various places <em>around</em> the canvas box instead of inside it or below it. (In my case, it was hidden in HTML hyperspace to the right of the box, and only appeared when I tab-ed around the page, which forced the container to scroll over to it.) The tweaks lock it and the submit button so that they're next to the flashing cursor, and formats them to look sort of like they belong there for minimal disruption while also making it semi-obvious what you're supposed to do.</p>

